{
  "_comment": [
    "Spike fixture for the Fixtures pane (sb-9z3). SIBLING FILE, not a section",
    "inside the document fixtures - the shape decision, and why:",
    "  A document fixture is an ADR-0001 envelope, and the spike's fromJson/1",
    "  mirrors the real decoder's strictness: it refuses a key the encoder would",
    "  never have written. The existing '_comment' keys already have to be",
    "  stripped before decoding for exactly that reason. Adding a 'runs' key to",
    "  the envelope would mean either a second thing to strip on every load or a",
    "  laxer decoder, and the strict check is what keeps encode(decode(b)) == b",
    "  honest. A run is also not part of the document: it is a fixture ABOUT one,",
    "  it has its own lifetime, and a host that ships documents from a database",
    "  will keep its fixtures somewhere else entirely. So: one file, keyed by",
    "  document id, fetched beside the document.",
    "",
    "EVERYTHING HERE IS MOCKED, per the campaign's D4 ruling: a run is a scripted",
    "sequence an author wrote, and a truth table's expected values are typed in.",
    "Nothing in the spike interprets a chart or evaluates a predicate. The runner",
    "REPLAYS; it does not compute. The pane says so on screen, because a fixture",
    "UI that looks like it is running the chart would be the single most",
    "misleading thing this spike could ship.",
    "",
    "Every block id referenced here exists in the matching document, and every",
    "datamodel path in a binding or a delta resolves in ../datamodel.json."
  ],
  "version": 1,
  "documents": {
    "bdoc_cp_demo": {
      "runs": [
        {
          "id": "run_cp_approved",
          "name": "Approved and captured",
          "description": "The happy path: validation passes, all three lanes clear, the outcome branch takes the approved arm, and the capture succeeds first try.",
          "expected": "pass",
          "steps": [
            {
              "label": "Take the payment request",
              "active": ["blk_cp_intake"],
              "event": "payment.requested",
              "deltas": [
                { "path": "amount_cents", "value": "42350" },
                { "path": "currency", "value": "\"USD\"" },
                { "path": "card.active", "value": "true" }
              ]
            },
            {
              "label": "Validation branch takes arm_valid",
              "active": ["blk_cp_validation"],
              "deltas": [{ "path": "validation.passed", "value": "true" }],
              "check": {
                "label": "arm_valid was taken",
                "result": "pass",
                "detail": "validation.passed AND amount_cents > 0 AND card.active all held."
              }
            },
            {
              "label": "Two lanes run side by side",
              "note": "The parallel block is live: the fraud lane is rating the transaction while the balance lane checks funds. Both cards are highlighted on the canvas.",
              "active": ["blk_cp_risk_rating", "blk_cp_balance"],
              "deltas": [
                { "path": "risk_rating", "value": "34" },
                { "path": "balance.available_cents", "value": "180000" }
              ]
            },
            {
              "label": "The 3DS lane joins",
              "note": "Three lanes active at once - the widest the parallel gets in this run.",
              "active": ["blk_cp_fraud_wait", "blk_cp_balance_wait", "blk_cp_three_ds"],
              "deltas": [{ "path": "three_ds.required", "value": "true" }]
            },
            {
              "label": "The cardholder completes the challenge",
              "active": ["blk_cp_three_ds_done"],
              "event": "card.three_ds_completed",
              "deltas": [
                { "path": "three_ds.completed", "value": "true" },
                { "path": "three_ds.status", "value": "\"authenticated\"" }
              ],
              "check": {
                "label": "the 3DS group resumed rather than timing out",
                "result": "pass",
                "detail": "The completion event reached the interrupt rail before the PT10M wait ran out."
              }
            },
            {
              "label": "Risk branch takes the low-risk arm",
              "active": ["blk_cp_risk_branch"],
              "deltas": [
                { "path": "fraud.verdict", "value": "\"clear\"" },
                { "path": "fraud.cleared", "value": "true" },
                { "path": "customer.verified", "value": "true" }
              ],
              "check": {
                "label": "arm_low_risk was taken, not arm_high_risk",
                "result": "pass",
                "detail": "risk_rating 34 < 40 and customer.verified held, so the high-risk arm never armed."
              }
            },
            {
              "label": "Authorize the card",
              "active": ["blk_cp_authorize"],
              "deltas": [
                { "path": "auth.approved", "value": "true" },
                { "path": "auth.code", "value": "\"A31842\"" }
              ]
            },
            {
              "label": "Outcome branch takes arm_approved",
              "active": ["blk_cp_outcome"],
              "check": {
                "label": "arm_approved was taken",
                "result": "pass",
                "detail": "auth.approved AND fraud.cleared AND balance.available_cents >= amount_cents."
              }
            },
            {
              "label": "Capture the funds",
              "active": ["blk_cp_capture"],
              "deltas": [
                { "path": "auth.captured", "value": "true" },
                { "path": "capture_attempts", "value": "1" }
              ],
              "check": {
                "label": "the retry arm was not taken",
                "result": "pass",
                "detail": "auth.captured == false no longer held, so the one-armed retry branch fell through."
              }
            },
            {
              "label": "Build and send the receipt",
              "active": ["blk_cp_receipt", "blk_cp_final_notify"],
              "note": "The tail runs to completion."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "run_cp_manual_review",
          "name": "Fraud flags it for manual review",
          "description": "The rating comes back high, the high-risk arm flags a human, and the outcome branch parks the work in the resumable group until a reviewer resolves it two days later.",
          "expected": "pass",
          "steps": [
            {
              "label": "Take the payment request",
              "active": ["blk_cp_intake"],
              "event": "payment.requested",
              "deltas": [{ "path": "amount_cents", "value": "980000" }]
            },
            {
              "label": "Validation passes",
              "active": ["blk_cp_validation"],
              "deltas": [{ "path": "validation.passed", "value": "true" }]
            },
            {
              "label": "The fraud and balance lanes run together",
              "active": ["blk_cp_risk_rating", "blk_cp_balance"],
              "deltas": [
                { "path": "risk_rating", "value": "88" },
                { "path": "balance.available_cents", "value": "1200000" }
              ]
            },
            {
              "label": "Risk branch takes the high-risk arm",
              "active": ["blk_cp_risk_branch"],
              "deltas": [{ "path": "fraud.verdict", "value": "\"review\"" }],
              "check": {
                "label": "arm_high_risk was taken",
                "result": "pass",
                "detail": "risk_rating 88 >= 70, so the first arm matched before the low-risk arm was tried."
              }
            },
            {
              "label": "Flag it for a human",
              "active": ["blk_cp_manual_flag"],
              "deltas": [{ "path": "fraud.cleared", "value": "false" }]
            },
            {
              "label": "Outcome branch takes arm_manual_review",
              "active": ["blk_cp_outcome"],
              "check": {
                "label": "arm_manual_review was taken, not arm_declined",
                "result": "pass",
                "detail": "fraud.verdict == 'review' and the backlog was under 50, and arm_declined's guard wanted verdict 'decline'."
              }
            },
            {
              "label": "Park it for a reviewer",
              "active": ["blk_cp_park"],
              "deltas": [
                { "path": "review.parked", "value": "true" },
                { "path": "review.queue", "value": "\"manual_review\"" }
              ]
            },
            {
              "label": "Two days pass",
              "active": ["blk_cp_manual_wait"],
              "note": "The resumable group holds deep history, so a resume lands back here rather than at the top of the arm."
            },
            {
              "label": "A reviewer approves it",
              "active": ["blk_cp_manual_resolved"],
              "event": "review.resolved",
              "deltas": [{ "path": "event.review_resolved.decision", "value": "\"approve\"" }],
              "check": {
                "label": "the guarded interrupt rule fired",
                "result": "pass",
                "detail": "decision == 'approve' AND review.parked both held."
              }
            },
            {
              "label": "Apply the reviewer's decision",
              "active": ["blk_cp_resolve"]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "run_cp_cancelled",
          "name": "Customer cancels mid-authorization",
          "description": "The customer cancels while the three lanes are still running. The authorization group's guarded interrupt rule abandons the work before anything is captured.",
          "expected": "pass",
          "steps": [
            {
              "label": "Take the payment request",
              "active": ["blk_cp_intake"],
              "event": "payment.requested"
            },
            {
              "label": "Validation passes",
              "active": ["blk_cp_validation"],
              "deltas": [{ "path": "validation.passed", "value": "true" }]
            },
            {
              "label": "The fraud and 3DS lanes are both waiting",
              "note": "Two lanes held open at once - this is the step the interrupt lands on.",
              "active": ["blk_cp_fraud_wait", "blk_cp_three_ds_wait"],
              "deltas": [{ "path": "auth.captured", "value": "false" }]
            },
            {
              "label": "The customer cancels",
              "active": ["blk_cp_cancelled"],
              "event": "customer.cancelled",
              "deltas": [
                { "path": "event.customer_cancelled.reason", "value": "\"customer_request\"" }
              ],
              "check": {
                "label": "the guarded rule fired and the group abandoned",
                "result": "pass",
                "detail": "reason == 'customer_request' AND auth.captured == false both held, so the rule took its abandon outcome."
              }
            },
            {
              "label": "Tell ops no outcome arm matched",
              "active": ["blk_cp_outcome_fallback"],
              "note": "The abandon skips the outcome arms, so the otherwise arm carries the notification."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "run_cp_three_ds_timeout",
          "name": "3DS never completes",
          "description": "The cardholder never answers the challenge. This fixture expects the PT15M authorization timeout to abandon the group - and the scripted run shows it does not, because the timeout rule's guard reads fraud.cleared, which the fraud lane never set either way.",
          "expected": "pass",
          "steps": [
            {
              "label": "Take the payment request",
              "active": ["blk_cp_intake"],
              "event": "payment.requested"
            },
            {
              "label": "Validation passes",
              "active": ["blk_cp_validation"],
              "deltas": [{ "path": "validation.passed", "value": "true" }]
            },
            {
              "label": "The challenge is sent",
              "active": ["blk_cp_three_ds"],
              "deltas": [{ "path": "three_ds.completed", "value": "false" }]
            },
            {
              "label": "The 3DS wait runs out",
              "active": ["blk_cp_three_ds_wait"],
              "note": "PT10M elapses with no completion event on the rail.",
              "check": {
                "label": "the 3DS group did not resume",
                "result": "pass",
                "detail": "No card.three_ds_completed event arrived, so the wait ran to its end."
              }
            },
            {
              "label": "The PT15M authorization timeout should fire",
              "active": ["blk_cp_authz_timeout"],
              "check": {
                "label": "the timeout rule abandons the authorization group",
                "result": "fail",
                "detail": "The rule's guard is three_ds.completed == false OR fraud.cleared == false. The fraud lane never ran, so fraud.cleared is unset rather than false - and this fixture records that the rule did not fire. Whether an unset boolean should read as false is a question for the expression language, not for this pane."
              }
            },
            {
              "label": "The group is still open",
              "active": ["blk_cp_authz"],
              "note": "The run stops here: with nothing on the rail able to fire, the authorization group has no way out."
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "tables": [
        {
          "id": "tbl_cp_risk",
          "blockId": "blk_cp_risk_branch",
          "name": "Risk rating branch",
          "description": "Which arm the fraud lane's branch takes. The arms are tried in order, so a row that satisfies both takes the first.",
          "columns": [
            { "key": "arm_high_risk", "label": "High risk", "expr": "risk_rating >= 70 OR fraud.verdict == 'review'" },
            { "key": "arm_low_risk", "label": "Low risk", "expr": "risk_rating < 40 AND customer.verified" },
            { "key": "otherwise", "label": "Otherwise", "expr": "no arm matched" }
          ],
          "paths": ["risk_rating", "fraud.verdict", "customer.verified"],
          "rows": [
            {
              "name": "Clear and low",
              "bindings": { "risk_rating": "34", "fraud.verdict": "'clear'", "customer.verified": "true" },
              "expected": { "arm_high_risk": false, "arm_low_risk": true, "otherwise": false }
            },
            {
              "name": "Rated high",
              "bindings": { "risk_rating": "88", "fraud.verdict": "'clear'", "customer.verified": "true" },
              "expected": { "arm_high_risk": true, "arm_low_risk": false, "otherwise": false }
            },
            {
              "name": "Flagged for review",
              "bindings": { "risk_rating": "12", "fraud.verdict": "'review'", "customer.verified": "true" },
              "expected": { "arm_high_risk": true, "arm_low_risk": false, "otherwise": false },
              "note": "Both arms' expressions hold. The high-risk arm is declared first, so it wins - which is the reason arm order is part of the config and not an implementation detail."
            },
            {
              "name": "Middling, unverified",
              "bindings": { "risk_rating": "55", "fraud.verdict": "'clear'", "customer.verified": "false" },
              "expected": { "arm_high_risk": false, "arm_low_risk": false, "otherwise": true },
              "note": "The gap between 40 and 70 is what the otherwise arm exists for."
            },
            {
              "name": "Low but unverified",
              "bindings": { "risk_rating": "12", "fraud.verdict": "'clear'", "customer.verified": "false" },
              "expected": { "arm_high_risk": false, "arm_low_risk": false, "otherwise": true },
              "note": "The AND is the whole difference: a low rating alone does not clear the arm."
            },
            {
              "name": "Declined outright",
              "bindings": { "risk_rating": "95", "fraud.verdict": "'decline'", "customer.verified": "true" },
              "expected": { "arm_high_risk": true, "arm_low_risk": false, "otherwise": false }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "tbl_cp_cancelled",
          "blockId": "blk_cp_cancelled",
          "name": "Customer-cancelled interrupt rule",
          "description": "Whether the authorization group's cancellation rule fires. It guards on the event payload and on whether the money has already moved.",
          "columns": [
            { "key": "cond", "label": "Rule fires", "expr": "event.customer_cancelled.reason == 'customer_request' AND auth.captured == false" }
          ],
          "paths": ["event.customer_cancelled.reason", "auth.captured"],
          "rows": [
            {
              "name": "Customer asked, nothing captured",
              "bindings": { "event.customer_cancelled.reason": "'customer_request'", "auth.captured": "false" },
              "expected": { "cond": true }
            },
            {
              "name": "Customer asked, already captured",
              "bindings": { "event.customer_cancelled.reason": "'customer_request'", "auth.captured": "true" },
              "expected": { "cond": false },
              "note": "The guard's whole job: once the funds have moved, cancelling is a refund and not an abandon."
            },
            {
              "name": "Duplicate request",
              "bindings": { "event.customer_cancelled.reason": "'duplicate'", "auth.captured": "false" },
              "expected": { "cond": false }
            },
            {
              "name": "Cancelled by timeout",
              "bindings": { "event.customer_cancelled.reason": "'timeout'", "auth.captured": "false" },
              "expected": { "cond": false },
              "note": "A timeout cancellation is the other rule's business - this one only answers a deliberate customer request."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "tbl_cp_outcome",
          "blockId": "blk_cp_outcome",
          "name": "Outcome branch",
          "description": "Three arms over the authorization result, tried in declaration order.",
          "columns": [
            { "key": "arm_approved", "label": "Approved", "expr": "auth.approved AND fraud.cleared AND balance.available_cents >= amount_cents" },
            { "key": "arm_declined", "label": "Declined", "expr": "fraud.verdict == 'decline' OR balance.available_cents < amount_cents" },
            { "key": "arm_manual_review", "label": "Manual review", "expr": "fraud.verdict == 'review' AND limits.manual_review_backlog < 50" }
          ],
          "paths": [
            "auth.approved",
            "fraud.cleared",
            "fraud.verdict",
            "balance.available_cents",
            "amount_cents",
            "limits.manual_review_backlog"
          ],
          "rows": [
            {
              "name": "Clean approval",
              "bindings": {
                "auth.approved": "true",
                "fraud.cleared": "true",
                "fraud.verdict": "'clear'",
                "balance.available_cents": "180000",
                "amount_cents": "42350",
                "limits.manual_review_backlog": "12"
              },
              "expected": { "arm_approved": true, "arm_declined": false, "arm_manual_review": false }
            },
            {
              "name": "Insufficient funds",
              "bindings": {
                "auth.approved": "true",
                "fraud.cleared": "true",
                "fraud.verdict": "'clear'",
                "balance.available_cents": "1000",
                "amount_cents": "42350",
                "limits.manual_review_backlog": "12"
              },
              "expected": { "arm_approved": false, "arm_declined": true, "arm_manual_review": false }
            },
            {
              "name": "Held for a reviewer",
              "bindings": {
                "auth.approved": "true",
                "fraud.cleared": "false",
                "fraud.verdict": "'review'",
                "balance.available_cents": "1200000",
                "amount_cents": "980000",
                "limits.manual_review_backlog": "12"
              },
              "expected": { "arm_approved": false, "arm_declined": false, "arm_manual_review": true }
            },
            {
              "name": "Review queue is full",
              "bindings": {
                "auth.approved": "true",
                "fraud.cleared": "false",
                "fraud.verdict": "'review'",
                "balance.available_cents": "1200000",
                "amount_cents": "980000",
                "limits.manual_review_backlog": "64"
              },
              "expected": { "arm_approved": false, "arm_declined": false, "arm_manual_review": false },
              "note": "No arm holds, so the otherwise arm notifies ops. A backlog cap that silently changes which arm is taken is exactly the kind of thing a truth table is for."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    "bdoc_signup_demo": {
      "runs": [
        {
          "id": "run_su_business",
          "name": "Business plan signup",
          "description": "The account is collected, the email verifies inside the day, and the plan branch routes to the company-details step.",
          "expected": "pass",
          "steps": [
            {
              "label": "Collect email and password",
              "active": ["blk_su_account"],
              "deltas": [{ "path": "signup.email", "value": "\"dana@example.com\"" }]
            },
            {
              "label": "Send the verification email",
              "active": ["blk_su_send_verification"]
            },
            {
              "label": "The customer verifies",
              "active": ["blk_su_verified"],
              "event": "signup.email_verified",
              "deltas": [{ "path": "signup.email_verified", "value": "true" }],
              "check": {
                "label": "the group resumed rather than waiting out PT24H",
                "result": "pass"
              }
            },
            {
              "label": "Plan branch takes arm_business",
              "active": ["blk_su_plan"],
              "deltas": [
                { "path": "signup.plan", "value": "\"business\"" },
                { "path": "signup.seats", "value": "8" }
              ],
              "check": {
                "label": "arm_business was taken",
                "result": "pass",
                "detail": "plan == 'business' AND seats > 1."
              }
            },
            {
              "label": "Collect the company details",
              "active": ["blk_su_company"]
            },
            {
              "label": "Create the workspace",
              "active": ["blk_su_provision"]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "run_su_abandoned",
          "name": "Verification never arrives",
          "description": "The customer never opens the email. This fixture expects the wizard to abandon; the scripted run records the PT24H wait falling through with no rule taking it, which is the gap the findings pane already warns about.",
          "expected": "pass",
          "steps": [
            {
              "label": "Collect email and password",
              "active": ["blk_su_account"]
            },
            {
              "label": "Send the verification email",
              "active": ["blk_su_send_verification"],
              "deltas": [{ "path": "signup.email_verified", "value": "false" }]
            },
            {
              "label": "The wait runs out",
              "active": ["blk_su_verify_wait"],
              "note": "PT24H with neither signup.email_verified nor signup.abandoned on the rail."
            },
            {
              "label": "Nothing abandons the wizard",
              "active": ["blk_su_verify"],
              "check": {
                "label": "the verify group ends without a resolution",
                "result": "fail",
                "detail": "Both interrupt rules wait for an event that never comes, and the group's body has run out. The document needs a timeout rule here - which is what the info-level finding on this group already says."
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "tables": [
        {
          "id": "tbl_su_plan",
          "blockId": "blk_su_plan",
          "name": "Plan branch",
          "description": "Which onboarding step a new account is routed to.",
          "columns": [
            { "key": "arm_business", "label": "Business", "expr": "signup.plan == 'business' AND signup.seats > 1" },
            { "key": "arm_personal", "label": "Personal", "expr": "signup.plan == 'personal' AND signup.email_verified" }
          ],
          "paths": ["signup.plan", "signup.seats", "signup.email_verified"],
          "rows": [
            {
              "name": "Team of eight",
              "bindings": { "signup.plan": "'business'", "signup.seats": "8", "signup.email_verified": "true" },
              "expected": { "arm_business": true, "arm_personal": false }
            },
            {
              "name": "Business, single seat",
              "bindings": { "signup.plan": "'business'", "signup.seats": "1", "signup.email_verified": "true" },
              "expected": { "arm_business": false, "arm_personal": false },
              "note": "A one-seat business plan falls to the otherwise arm, which nudges them to pick a plan again. Probably wrong, and only visible as a row."
            },
            {
              "name": "Personal, verified",
              "bindings": { "signup.plan": "'personal'", "signup.seats": "1", "signup.email_verified": "true" },
              "expected": { "arm_business": false, "arm_personal": true }
            },
            {
              "name": "Personal, unverified",
              "bindings": { "signup.plan": "'personal'", "signup.seats": "1", "signup.email_verified": "false" },
              "expected": { "arm_business": false, "arm_personal": false }
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  }
}
